  "claim": "The director Jonathan Demme presented the 74-minute unedited Made in Texas at a theater in Lower Manhattan which featured work from the filmmaker Dziga Vertov, also known as Denis Kaufman.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Collective for Living Cinema. Sentence: The Collective for Living Cinema was an outpost of avant-garde cinema located on White Street in Lower Manhattan in the United States of America.\nPage: Dziga Vertov. Sentence: Dziga Vertov (Russian: Дзига Вертов ; born David Abelevich Kaufman, Russian: Дави́д А́белевич Ка́уфман , and also known as Denis Kaufman; 2 January 1896 – 12 February 1954) was a Soviet pioneer documentary film and newsreel director, as well as a cinema theorist.\nPage: Made in Texas. Sentence: In October 1981, director Jonathan Demme presented the Made in Texas - New Films From Austin series at the Collective for Living Cinema in New York City.",
