        "original_id": "adcfff16-eaf5-58bd-b38e-4daf8918a949",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Collective for Living Cinema\n- People: Dziga Vertov, Jonathan Demme\n- Projects: Made in Texas\n- Places: White Street, Lower Manhattan, New York City, United States of America\n- Roles: documentary film director, newsreel director, cinema theorist\n\nFacts:\n- Dziga Vertov was born David Abelevich Kaufman, was also known as Denis Kaufman, and lived from 2 January 1896 to 12 February 1954.\n- Dziga Vertov was a Soviet pioneer documentary film director, newsreel director, and cinema theorist.\n- In October 1981, director Jonathan Demme presented the Made in Texas – New Films From Austin series at the Collective for Living Cinema in New York City.\n- The Collective for Living Cinema was an outpost of avant-garde cinema located on White Street in Lower Manhattan in the United States of America.",
